      "reviewed": true,
      "severity": "P1",
      "xp": 120,
      "title": "Duplicate event IDs after NTP step",
      "brief": "An NTP correction stepped one Snowflake worker's clock back 800 ms. It re-minted IDs for timestamps it had already used, and 3,100 Kafka events were deduplicated away as repeats.",
      "constraint": "The worker must never emit the same ID twice, even when its clock jumps.",
      "question": "What change stops the duplicates?",
